Epilogue: The Return to the Graph

The four of them stood before the graph again.

The line remained frozen in its upward arc, rising gently at first and then sharply towards the top-right corner.

The Optimist looked at it.

“It represents compounding capability.”

The Pessimist folded her arms.

“It represents power moving faster than accountability.”

The Sceptic leaned closer.

“It represents whatever the vertical axis measures.”

Dave wiped a fingerprint from the glass.

“It represents a good meeting.”

He looked towards the factory.

“Who’s coming down to help me bleed the air out of the line?”

Nobody moved.

The Optimist wanted to finish explaining the feedback loop.

The Pessimist was considering what the line meant for democratic control.

The Sceptic had begun searching for the original dataset.

Dave put the spanner back into his pocket and walked towards the bay.

The graph may have been right.

The courier was still due at seven.
